# Template for the local personal-data denylist used by scripts/check-no-personal-data.mjs.
#
# Copy this file to `.personal-data-denylist` in the repository root and replace the placeholder
# lines with your own values. That file is git-ignored and must never be committed: the check
# refuses to run when git would commit it. Never put real values in this template.
#
# In CI, store the same content in a repository secret and expose it as OPENCODE_UNITY_DENYLIST.
# You can also keep the file elsewhere and pass --denylist <file> or OPENCODE_UNITY_DENYLIST_FILE.
#
# Format:
# - one term per line, at least 3 characters;
# - lines starting with '#' are comments;
# - terms match file contents and file paths as substrings, ignoring case and diacritics;
#   '\' and '/' are treated as the same separator, so a path matches in every spelling;
# - 'allow: <exact string>' removes that public string before matching, for example the public
#   repository URL when your account name is also a denylist term.
#
# Findings print the entry number, never the value.

# Your real name and any spelling of it
Jane Placeholder

# Your OS user name, machine name and account handles
placeholder-user
PLACEHOLDER-PC

# Your e-mail addresses (addresses outside example domains are already caught by a built-in rule)
jane.placeholder@example.invalid

# Local paths that identify you or your machine
D:/Work/placeholder-projects

# Game, studio, company or client names that must not appear in this generic project
Placeholder Game Title
Placeholder Studio

# allow: github.com/placeholder-user/opencode-unity
